			"notes": "This is the first full release of the Java Soft Inversion mod.\n\n**What's Included?**\n\n* All torches can now be supported on the sides of extended pistons and no longer pop off.\n* Redstone torches attached to the top or non-head sides of pistons will now depower if the piston extends or is powered but can’t extend.\n* Redstone dust will now connect to non-head sides of pistons.\n* Added the `enable_qc` gamerule (`true` by default), which controls whether pistons, droppers, and dispensers are affected by QC.\n* Added `enable_soft_inversion` gamerule (`true` by default) to control whether redstone torches can be depowered by an extended/powered piston.\n\n*Fixes*\n\n* Fixed [MC-94003](https://bugs.mojang.com/browse/MC/issues/MC-94003) - Pistons now have a hitbox when in motion, making it easier to break pistons when they are spamming on and off and preventing placing blocks through the piston.\n\n---\n\n**Changes since 1.0.0-rc.1+mc26.3:**\n\n* Updated Fabric and NeoForge to the latest versions and moved to NeoLoom 1.18 from 1.17."
		},
